{"term":"migrate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d80ee55c15d447bf84","definition":"To relocate periodically from one region to another, usually according to the seasons.","example":"Twice a year the geese migrate — from Florida to Canada and back again.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["abmigrate","comigrate","countermigrate","demigrate","electromigrated","emigrate","immigrate","migratable","migration","migrative","migrator","migratory","mismigrate","mismigrated","nonmigrated","nonmigrating","outmigrate","overmigrate","remigrate","transmigrate","unmigrate","unmigrated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/migrate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0fee659f07d2cca533","definition":"To change one's geographic pattern of habitation.","example":"Many groups had migrated to western Europe from the plains of eastern Europe.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["abmigrate","comigrate","countermigrate","demigrate","electromigrated","emigrate","immigrate","migratable","migration","migrative","migrator","migratory","mismigrate","mismigrated","nonmigrated","nonmigrating","outmigrate","overmigrate","remigrate","transmigrate","unmigrate","unmigrated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/migrate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f4fe1ec0772145c56","definition":"To change habitations across a border; to move from one country or political region to another.","example":"To escape persecution, they migrated to a neutral country.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["abmigrate","comigrate","countermigrate","demigrate","electromigrated","emigr